# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs: pyproject.toml,
# README.md, src/ and docker/. Everything below is either secret, host-specific,
# huge, or irrelevant to a Linux runtime image.

# --- secrets & local configuration ---
# A pattern without a slash is matched against the top level only, so a bare
# `.env.*` never covered docker/.env.migration — which holds a real Neo4j
# password and seven API keys. `**/` is what makes the rule recursive.
# The allow-list is `**/.env*.example` (not just `.env.example`) so every
# template survives: .env.windows.example, docker/.env.migration.example, etc.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env*.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
config/mcp-config*.json

# --- version control & agent state ---
.git
.gitattributes
.githooks
.claude
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# --- local Python environments & caches ---
# Same top-level-only caveat as above. Before `**/` was added, all 46 nested
# __pycache__ directories under src/oh_memos were copied into the image: 8.4 MB
# of dead weight (66% of src/oh_memos), half of it cpython-312 bytecode that a
# python:3.11 base can never load. Worse, each .pyc embeds the absolute
# co_filename it was compiled from, publishing the build host's local path.
# Nothing loaded them — the runtime imports from site-packages — so this was
# pure bloat plus a path leak, not a correctness bug.
# The cache directory names below stay top-level-only on purpose: `**/data` and
# `**/runtime` would match the real package directories src/oh_memos/data and
# src/oh_memos/data/runtime.
.venv
conda_venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
.memos

# --- runtime data (must come from volumes, never from the image) ---
data
storage
logs
backups
snapshots
runtime
# The API image copies src/oh_memos only, but keep these out of the context so a
# 2GB local runtime never has to be uploaded to the daemon in the first place.
src/bin
src/logs
src/.memos
src/.env*

# --- node / MCP server (runs on the host via npx, not in this image) ---
mcp-server-node
node_modules

# --- not needed at runtime ---
tests
evaluation
examples
docs
tools
oh-memos-cli
oh-memos-deploy
mcp-server
project-memory
scripts
VENV_scripts
Makefile
*.bat
*.cmd
*.ps1
*.vbs
docker/docker-compose*.yml
